# Production API URL — used by `next build` (e.g. on Vercel).
# Local dev uses .env.local instead (localhost). This value is a public
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* setting (already visible in the client bundle), so it is
# safe to commit.
#
# The API moved from Render to Vercel. This file still pointed at the old
# Render host, so every production build kept baking that URL into the
# client bundle — the live site was calling Render no matter what the Vercel
# dashboard said. Deleting the Render service would have taken the site down.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://car-number1-api.vercel.app/api
